    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n317" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγαμέμνων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Agamemnon,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, etc.: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγαμέμνονος δαίς,</span>
			of a fatal feast, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1507.60
			</span></i>:—also epith. of Zeus at Sparta, Staphylus
				Hist.<i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				168.10
			</span></i>.—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγᾰμεμνόνεος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έα</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαλμο-όνειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εία</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ειον</span>, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαλμο-όνιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ία</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>: Patron.</div>
